inical care"},"cms-f0688":{"code":"F-0688","title":"Provide appropriate care for a resident to maintain and/or improve range of motion (ROM), limited ROM and/or mobility, unless a decline is for a medical reason.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0692":{"code":"F-0692","title":"Provide enough food/fluids to maintain a resident's health.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0694":{"code":"F-0694","title":"Provide for the safe, appropriate administration of IV fluids for a resident when needed.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0695":{"code":"F-0695","title":"Provide safe and appropriate respiratory care for a resident when needed.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0700":{"code":"F-0700","title":"Try different approaches before using a bed rail.  If a bed rail is needed, the facility must (1) assess a resident for safety risk; (2) review these risks and benefits with the resident/representative; (3) get informed consent; and (4) Correctly install and maintain the bed rail.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0756":{"code":"F-0756","title":"Ensure a licensed pharmacist perform a monthly drug regimen review, including the medical chart, following irregularity reporting guidelines in developed policies and procedures.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0812":{"code":"F-0812","title":"Procure food from sources approved or considered satisfactory and store, prepare, distribute and serve food in accordance with professional standards.","category":"Nutrition and Dietary Deficiencies","concept":"